{
  "summary": "Serializes pending private broadcast transactions to `privatebroadcast.dat` on node shutdown and reloads them on startup when `-privatebroadcast` is enabled. It adds methods to inspect broadcast state and hooks into the node initialization and shutdown sequence, deleting the file after load.",
  "problem": "Private broadcast transactions exist solely in memory inside the peer manager. If a node shuts down or restarts before completing private broadcasts over Tor or I2P, those pending transactions are dropped and will never be broadcast.",
  "evidence": [
   "Description notes: 'Currently private broadcast transactions are stored in peer manager and do not persist over restarts. A submitted transaction can be lost if the node restarts before it is privately broadcast.'",
   "Follow-up to #29415 which added the private broadcast mechanism."
  ],
